. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+{e}^{1/2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈3.898\\,721\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y≈3.898\\,721.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\  & ≈2(3.898\\,721)+{e}^{1}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & ≈11.515\\,724\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, rounded to $2$ decimal places, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈3.90,\\,y(1)≈11.52.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d5017afb8ec1f436c3f7424030891fe152f921a61e95e4ea505ad341ad43da8"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4d0e92deeea4b5101cd2da929cea4146a3b1d248358a43bc4637afd491d673da"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d5017afb8ec1f436c3f7424030891fe152f921a61e95e4ea505ad341ad43da8"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.00"] ["math" "3.73"] ["math" "3.90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d5017afb8ec1f436c3f7424030891fe152f921a61e95e4ea505ad341ad43da8"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.90"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d5017afb8ec1f436c3f7424030891fe152f921a61e95e4ea505ad341ad43da8"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069978/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d5017afb8ec1f436c3f7424030891fe152f921a61e95e4ea505ad341ad43da8"} {"question" "q-339722" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11.52"] ["math" "9.33"] ["math" "9.95"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/hom